# Network Security Lab

## Objective

The objective of this lab is to understand basic network
security concepts and how security controls help protect
systems and data.

## Topics Covered

- Network security
- IP addresses
- Ports and protocols
- Firewalls
- Authentication
- Network threats
- Security best practices

## What I Learned

I learned that network security helps protect computers,
networks, and data from unauthorized access.

I also learned that firewalls, strong authentication,
and secure network configurations are important parts
of network security.

## Security Best Practices

- Use strong passwords
- Enable multi-factor authentication
- Keep systems updated
- Use firewalls
- Secure Wi-Fi networks
- Monitor network activity
- Avoid unknown links and downloads

## Conclusion

This lab helped me understand the basic principles of
network security and the importance of protecting
systems and networks from security threats.
